= Managing Connected Apps
ifndef::env-site,env-github[]
include::_attributes.adoc[]
endif::[]
:imagesdir: ../assets/images/

Connected apps are applications that allow external applications to securely interact with the Anypoint Platform APIs by providing controlled access to its resources using OAuth 2.0 authentication protocols, without the need to share user credentials directly. For more information, see xref:access-management::connected-apps-overview.adoc[].

When an API created using a connected app is published to Exchange, the API’s owner is automatically set as the owner of the connected app. 

Control whether or not to assign owner roles when creating applications using a connected app to avoid going over the maximum role xref:access-management::troubleshooting-anypoint-platform-access.adoc#access-management-limits[limit].

. From the navigation bar, select *Settings* and select *Manage Connected Apps and Asset Deletion*.
. In *Connected Application Owner Configuration*, enable or disable the option.
+
If enabled, when creating a new asset, roles aren't assigned to connected app owners. If disabled, roles are assigned by default.

